WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.800
From ingredients to portion sizes,

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.166
we wanted to know all the differences

00:00:03.166 --> 00:00:05.066
between Shake Shack and In-N-Out.

00:00:05.066 --> 00:00:06.833
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:06.833 --> 00:00:08.866
This isn't a standard "Food Wars" episode.

00:00:08.866 --> 00:00:11.300
We're pitting two different
US chains against each other,

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.200
which means we're going to do
things slightly differently.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.866
We're going to be keeping score as we go,

00:00:14.866 --> 00:00:17.100
and at the end, we'll decide objectively

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.466
which chain is the best.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.033
Here's everything you can
get at an In-N-Out Burger.

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:24.566
Here's everything you
can get at a Shake Shack.

00:00:24.566 --> 00:00:25.500
I'm going to make a case

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.966
on why I think the
In-N-Out menu is better.

00:00:27.966 --> 00:00:29.333
I've been to a lot of In-N-Outs,

00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:31.033
I've been to a lot of Shake Shacks,

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:32.866
but today, I am going to make the case

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:36.500
as to why I think the Shake
Shack menu is just better.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.766
But the points will be awarded
by our independent referee,

00:00:39.766 --> 00:00:41.466
which should be Harry

00:00:41.466 --> 00:00:43.500
popping in somewhere.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.900
You are absolutely right, Nico.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:45.766
To make sure this is fair,

00:00:45.766 --> 00:00:47.733
I'm going to step in
as the neutral referee.

00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:48.900
I want a nice, clean fight.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:49.733
Let's go.

00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:51.933
Obviously these are two
different restaurants,

00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:54.100
so everything is going to be an exclusive.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.866
But we're going to start
off with the burgers.

00:00:55.866 --> 00:00:57.966
The Shake Shack burgers consist of

00:00:57.966 --> 00:01:00.666
the cheeseburger, hamburger,

00:01:00.666 --> 00:01:03.033
the ShackBurger, which
is my personal favorite,

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:07.100
bacon cheeseburger, the
SmokeShack, the shroom burger,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.600
the Shack Stack, which is a shroom burger

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.200
and a regular burger stacked
on top of each other.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.466
I am not the biggest fan of mushrooms,

00:01:14.466 --> 00:01:16.333
but it looks pretty good.

00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:18.833
This is a huge burger.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.400
The shroom part of this
Shack Stack looks empty.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.266
It looks really empty in there.

00:01:28.266 --> 00:01:29.533
It looks hollow.

00:01:29.533 --> 00:01:31.200
It tastes really, really good.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.666
I'm very surprised, because I
really don't like mushrooms,

00:01:33.666 --> 00:01:36.666
but this works really well
with the regular patty.

00:01:36.666 --> 00:01:38.333
Because I'm having a hard time

00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:40.233
finding the mushroom in the Shack Stack,

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:43.766
I do kind of want to taste
the shroom burger on its own

00:01:43.766 --> 00:01:46.733
to see if it's any more obvious.

00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:50.500
The shroom burger on its own is definitely

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.066
a lot more mushroomy,

00:01:52.066 --> 00:01:54.633
but still, I feel like
the main flavor you get

00:01:54.633 --> 00:01:57.433
is of whatever this crispy coating is,

00:01:57.433 --> 00:01:59.600
which tastes pretty delicious.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.866
In-N-Out has fewer burger options,

00:02:01.866 --> 00:02:03.633
but they also have a not-so-secret menu

00:02:03.633 --> 00:02:04.766
with even more burgers.

00:02:04.766 --> 00:02:08.400
These first three are on
the official In-N-Out menu.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.533
Starting down here, we got the hamburger,

00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:11.900
and of course, cheeseburger.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.200
This to me is probably
what I get every time.

00:02:16.466 --> 00:02:18.200
I like the cheese with the onions.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.766
Yeah.

00:02:19.766 --> 00:02:22.233
Then the Double-Double, or
the double cheeseburger.

00:02:22.233 --> 00:02:24.300
Next, we have the Veggie Shack.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.233
I also want to take a bite of this.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.133
I feel like this is just
another one of those cases

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:32.333
where I'm not really
getting the full flavor

00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:33.900
of the patty, because everything else

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.166
is kind of overwhelming.

00:02:35.166 --> 00:02:38.833
The pickles and the fried
onions is mainly what I taste.

00:02:38.833 --> 00:02:41.133
Then we have the avocado bacon burger.

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:43.900
Believe it or not, there
is avocado in here.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.533
We also have a new burger,

00:02:45.533 --> 00:02:47.600
which is the spicy ShackMeister.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.400
It has cherry peppers in it,

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.700
some fried onion, and a seasoning.

00:02:53.966 --> 00:02:55.966
I don't think I know anything
about cherry peppers.

00:02:55.966 --> 00:02:58.366
They kind of taste a little bit pickled.

00:02:58.366 --> 00:03:00.833
There's just like a
little brininess to them

00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:02.566
that's actually pretty tasty.

00:03:02.566 --> 00:03:05.566
Now the not-so-secret
menu has the double meat.

00:03:05.566 --> 00:03:07.400
That's two beef patties.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.333
You do protein style,

00:03:08.333 --> 00:03:11.466
which replaces the buns with lettuce.

00:03:11.466 --> 00:03:14.033
animal-style, which, animal-style is

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:17.600
Thousand Island dressing,
diced onions, and pickles.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:18.666
I don't like pickles,

00:03:19.633 --> 00:03:22.233
but Thousand Island
dressing and diced onions,

00:03:22.233 --> 00:03:23.066
let's go.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.566
The vinegariness of the pickles

00:03:27.566 --> 00:03:30.366
with the Thousand Island and the onions,

00:03:30.366 --> 00:03:31.200
very nice.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.066
Very nice addition.

00:03:32.066 --> 00:03:33.933
And, as seen before,

00:03:33.933 --> 00:03:34.766
the 3x3

00:03:34.766 --> 00:03:35.666
and the 4x4,

00:03:35.666 --> 00:03:38.833
which is three patties of
meat, three slices of cheese,

00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:40.033
or four patties of meat,

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:43.033
four slices of cheese.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:43.933
Come on, guys.

00:03:45.766 --> 00:03:47.566
If you're getting this,
you're just showing off.

00:03:48.966 --> 00:03:50.866
I would argue you're better off

00:03:50.866 --> 00:03:54.033
getting two double cheeseburgers
than the four-by-four.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.233
I think Shake Shack gets one point

00:03:55.233 --> 00:03:56.300
for having more options.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.066
I think selection is a good thing.

00:03:58.066 --> 00:04:00.033
I'm almost tempted to
deduct a point from In-N-Out

00:04:00.033 --> 00:04:00.900
for that lettuce burger,

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.400
but I'll let it slide for now.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.700
Apparently a quad burger with four patties

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.000
existed at some point

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.166
on the unofficial Shake Shack secret menu.

00:04:08.166 --> 00:04:10.900
The option to add more
patties seems to be gone now,

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:13.533
so we're just going to
Frankenstein our own quad burger.

00:04:14.733 --> 00:04:17.533
All right, I can do it. OK.

00:04:17.533 --> 00:04:19.433
Don't look at me.

00:04:19.433 --> 00:04:20.966
Everyone turn around.

00:04:24.233 --> 00:04:25.700
I would never order that.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.166
That's just like, way too much meat

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:29.866
to be enjoyable right now.

00:04:29.866 --> 00:04:33.566
But it is possible.

00:04:33.566 --> 00:04:35.533
Anything is possible.

00:04:35.533 --> 00:04:37.533
Moving on to the chicken options.

00:04:37.533 --> 00:04:40.566
Shake Shack offers the
avocado bacon chicken,

00:04:40.566 --> 00:04:42.600
the Chicken Shack, the hot chicken,

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:44.066
and chicken bites,

00:04:44.066 --> 00:04:45.733
which look really, really good.

00:04:45.733 --> 00:04:48.166
I actually haven't seen
a spicy chicken sandwich

00:04:48.166 --> 00:04:49.633
on their menu for a while.

00:04:49.633 --> 00:04:51.866
I feel like this is a recent addition,

00:04:51.866 --> 00:04:53.600
so I do want to taste it.

00:04:57.566 --> 00:04:58.666
That's a really good chicken sandwich.

00:04:58.666 --> 00:04:59.633
I feel like a lot of people

00:04:59.633 --> 00:05:01.466
sleep on the chicken
options at Shake Shack.

00:05:01.466 --> 00:05:03.366
They're all really, really good.

00:05:03.366 --> 00:05:06.566
And I do feel like this looks more filling

00:05:06.566 --> 00:05:07.900
than their regular burgers.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:10.333
It just looks like a
hardy piece of chicken.

00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:12.200
I do want to try one of
the chicken bites, too.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.200
I'm going to use some Shack sauce.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.200
I'm a dipper.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.633
I need sauce always.

00:05:18.733 --> 00:05:21.166
They're good. They're just a lot saltier

00:05:21.166 --> 00:05:22.633
than the chicken patties

00:05:22.633 --> 00:05:24.200
in any of their chicken sandwiches,

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.533
which is confusing to me.

00:05:25.533 --> 00:05:26.800
If you're in the mood for chicken,

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.033
do not come to In-N-Out,

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:29.166
because they have none.

00:05:29.166 --> 00:05:32.533
In-N-Out hasn't changed
the menu since 1976,

00:05:32.533 --> 00:05:33.800
so I don't think they're planning on

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.833
adding chicken to the menu anytime soon.

00:05:35.833 --> 00:05:36.866
In-N-Out's small menu

00:05:36.866 --> 00:05:38.900
seems to be working out for
them really well, though.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.166
They make everything fresh,

00:05:40.166 --> 00:05:43.133
so it probably helps simplifying
day-to-day operations.

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:45.833
Plus, bigger menus means increased costs.

00:05:45.833 --> 00:05:47.000
You made a pretty good case there, Joe,

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.600
but I think Shake Shack
still gets one point

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:49.933
for having chicken options.

00:05:49.933 --> 00:05:52.200
We also have a couple non-burger options.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.633
There's a grilled cheese and a BLT.

00:05:54.633 --> 00:05:57.533
I love when a restaurant
makes their sandwiches

00:05:57.533 --> 00:05:59.566
with grilled burger buns.

00:05:59.566 --> 00:06:00.933
The grilled cheese with the burger buns

00:06:00.933 --> 00:06:01.900
is very elite to me,

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.200
and I don't know why.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.033
It just tastes really good.

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:06.600
It's extra buttery, extra delicious.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:07.433
I don't know what it is.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.066
In-N-Out also has a grilled cheese.

00:06:10.066 --> 00:06:11.333
It's pretty much the only
vegetarian menu item they have

00:06:11.333 --> 00:06:12.666
that isn't a side or a milkshake.

00:06:12.666 --> 00:06:14.533
If you're not in the mood for a burger,

00:06:14.533 --> 00:06:16.466
Shake Shack also has hot dogs.

00:06:16.466 --> 00:06:18.233
They started out as a hot dog place,

00:06:18.233 --> 00:06:19.600
so it's kind of cool that they've

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.066
held onto the tradition
of making hot dogs.

00:06:22.066 --> 00:06:22.900
You'll notice that they

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.300
slice their hot dogs
right down the middle.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.366
This method helps cook
the hot dogs more evenly.

00:06:28.366 --> 00:06:30.666
I personally love the split hot dogs.

00:06:30.666 --> 00:06:33.100
I love all the
caramelization that you get.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.866
But I don't think Joe is a fan.

00:06:34.866 --> 00:06:36.066
Yeah, split hot dog, I hate it.

00:06:36.066 --> 00:06:36.900
Completely pointless.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.700
It doesn't change the taste of it at all.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:40.233
Flag on the play.

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:41.733
Look at the state of that hot dog.

00:06:41.733 --> 00:06:42.600
No points for that one.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:45.766
For sides, we've got fries, cheese fries,

00:06:45.766 --> 00:06:48.733
bacon cheese fries,
spicy fries with ranch,

00:06:48.733 --> 00:06:51.233
and spicy cheese fries with ranch.

00:06:51.233 --> 00:06:52.700
These are new to the menu.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.200
I don't know if they're going
to be permanent forever,

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.933
but we were able to get them today.

00:06:56.933 --> 00:07:00.433
We as a nation just cannot stay
away from the ranch, can we?

00:07:00.433 --> 00:07:03.766
I've never even heard of
ranch and fries together,

00:07:03.766 --> 00:07:07.466
not even as a dipping
sauce with regular fries.

00:07:07.466 --> 00:07:08.766
Oh my God, no.

00:07:08.766 --> 00:07:10.033
I've never heard of that.

00:07:10.033 --> 00:07:11.266
I kind of want to try the fry

00:07:11.266 --> 00:07:12.933
without the ranch first. Hold on.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.933
It's that same spicy seasoning

00:07:15.933 --> 00:07:18.233
that we saw on that chicken sandwich

00:07:18.233 --> 00:07:19.700
and on one of the burgers.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:20.933
It is really spicy

00:07:20.933 --> 00:07:24.266
when it's so liberally applied.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.066
I do think that these fries

00:07:29.066 --> 00:07:31.866
are definitely better with
the ranch than without it,

00:07:31.866 --> 00:07:34.366
and it also helps tame
some of that spiciness.

00:07:34.366 --> 00:07:35.766
This is interesting.

00:07:35.766 --> 00:07:38.500
I don't know if I'm fully sold
on dipping fries in ranch,

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:39.900
but it doesn't taste bad.

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:41.400
In-N-Out does have fries,

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:42.233
and I'm sorry,

00:07:42.233 --> 00:07:45.166
but this is where In-N-Out
suddenly becomes not so great.

00:07:45.166 --> 00:07:48.266
You can get various customizations

00:07:48.266 --> 00:07:49.633
and secret menu ones.

00:07:49.633 --> 00:07:52.000
The fries, ugh. Just avoid them.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.233
Right here are the regular fries.

00:07:54.233 --> 00:07:55.166
Let's take a bite.

00:07:56.566 --> 00:07:57.400
Terrible.

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:59.100
Also get the animal-style fries.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.033
Onion, Thousand Island, cheese.

00:08:04.333 --> 00:08:05.166
Better.

00:08:05.166 --> 00:08:07.066
You can also ask for fries well done,

00:08:07.066 --> 00:08:08.700
where I think they cook them twice

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.866
or just make them extra crispy.

00:08:10.866 --> 00:08:11.700
They're not,

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:14.133
the problem is they're not very salty.

00:08:14.133 --> 00:08:15.633
You also got cheese fries.

00:08:17.733 --> 00:08:19.366
Not bad.

00:08:19.366 --> 00:08:20.866
Yeah, because there's cheese on them.

00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:22.300
You can also get something
called roadkill fries,

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:24.400
which is animal-style plus a beef patty.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.233
I asked there,

00:08:25.233 --> 00:08:26.733
and the guy said he can
give you animal-style

00:08:26.733 --> 00:08:27.566
and a beef patty,

00:08:27.566 --> 00:08:29.533
I got to make it myself, whatever.

00:08:29.533 --> 00:08:31.400
Also, lemon pepper
fries, where it's, again,

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.433
just you take a lemon wedge

00:08:33.433 --> 00:08:34.433
and squeeze it on your fries,

00:08:34.433 --> 00:08:36.000
and then pepper them.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:37.733
I'm not doing that.

00:08:37.733 --> 00:08:39.066
I'm not the first person to say it:

00:08:39.066 --> 00:08:40.733
These fries are not good.

00:08:40.733 --> 00:08:41.833
I like the animal-style,

00:08:41.833 --> 00:08:42.800
and I like the cheese fries,

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:45.666
because they both have
cheese on it and sauce

00:08:45.666 --> 00:08:46.500
and fun stuff.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.366
But, yeah, these fries,

00:08:49.366 --> 00:08:50.200
not only are they weak,

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:52.400
but they're bland and dry.

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:55.000
No good.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:55.966
Joe, you're not doing a very good job

00:08:55.966 --> 00:08:57.466
of advocating for In-N-Out there.

00:08:57.466 --> 00:08:58.766
I'm going to have to give
Shake Shack the point.

00:08:58.766 --> 00:08:59.866
Those fries look better.

00:08:59.866 --> 00:09:02.266
It's time for sauce talk.

00:09:02.266 --> 00:09:03.133
Sauce talk.

00:09:03.133 --> 00:09:04.066
Sauce talk.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:10.800
For exclusive sauces, we
only have the Shack sauce.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.900
The real sauce recipe is a secret,

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.600
but they give a close-enough recipe

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:16.066
in the Shake Shack cookbook.

00:09:16.066 --> 00:09:18.333
This sauce contains Hellmann's mayonnaise,

00:09:18.333 --> 00:09:20.300
Dijon mustard, Heinz ketchup,

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:22.833
kosher dill pickling brine - interesting -

00:09:22.833 --> 00:09:24.066
and cayenne pepper.

00:09:24.066 --> 00:09:25.500
I think the Shake Shack sauce

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.900
is a really good burger sauce

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:29.766
that just works well with any food.

00:09:29.766 --> 00:09:32.300
In-N-Out has their own
special sauce known as spread.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:33.566
And the recipe is top secret,

00:09:33.566 --> 00:09:35.900
but there are a bunch of
copycat recipes out there.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.933
That is what's part of the animal-style,

00:09:37.933 --> 00:09:39.666
and we saw it on some
of the burgers earlier.

00:09:39.666 --> 00:09:42.333
It is possible the sauce contains mayo,

00:09:42.333 --> 00:09:44.266
ketchup, sweet pickle relish,

00:09:44.266 --> 00:09:45.733
and white-wine vinegar.

00:09:45.733 --> 00:09:48.700
It tastes exactly like
Thousand Island dressing.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:50.366
Those sauces just sound the same.

00:09:50.366 --> 00:09:51.400
You can both have a point.

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:53.466
As for soft drinks, Shake Shack offers

00:09:53.466 --> 00:09:56.533
Coke, Diet Coke, Dr Pepper, Fanta orange,

00:09:56.533 --> 00:10:00.000
Sprite, Ginger Ale, Coke
Zero, Draft root beer,

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.266
Shack-made lemonade, 50/50 lemonade,

00:10:02.266 --> 00:10:04.100
which is half ice tea, half lemonade,

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:05.300
strawberry lemonade,

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.166
and dragonfruit pomegranate lemonade,

00:10:07.166 --> 00:10:08.933
which you can order caffeinated.

00:10:08.933 --> 00:10:11.800
And you can also get organic
Harney &amp; Sons ice tea,

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:14.100
and Honest Kids organic apple juice.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:16.100
I am a lemonade lover.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:17.033
I really like the lemonade at Shake Shack.

00:10:17.033 --> 00:10:18.833
But what I am interested in trying

00:10:18.833 --> 00:10:21.600
is this new harvest berry lemonade.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:22.800
These are caffeinated.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.566
They have a few different flavors.

00:10:24.566 --> 00:10:26.833
And they have all these odd ingredients

00:10:26.833 --> 00:10:29.033
that I've just never heard put together.

00:10:29.033 --> 00:10:30.900
Here are those ingredients.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.200
Cinnamon was the ingredient

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.100
that really jumped out at me,

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:35.200
because I'm like, cinnamon in my lemonade?

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.300
That's kooky.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:40.466
It has a slightly medicinal taste

00:10:40.466 --> 00:10:42.466
that reminds me of tea,

00:10:42.466 --> 00:10:44.033
but not a fun iced tea.

00:10:44.033 --> 00:10:45.966
Just when you're sick
and you're drinking tea.

00:10:45.966 --> 00:10:47.300
But it's not bad.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:49.500
I can definitely taste the cinnamon,

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.333
and it's a little off-putting,

00:10:51.333 --> 00:10:52.266
because of the tartness,

00:10:52.266 --> 00:10:53.266
and then I get the cinnamon.

00:10:53.266 --> 00:10:54.100
I don't know.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:57.200
It's not super working
well together for me,

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:58.533
but it's not bad.

00:10:58.533 --> 00:11:00.366
At In-N-Out, you have an option of Coke,

00:11:00.366 --> 00:11:03.166
Diet Coke, 7-Up, Dr Pepper, root beer,

00:11:03.166 --> 00:11:06.866
pink lemonade, and Minute
Maid zero-sugar lemonade.

00:11:06.866 --> 00:11:09.633
You can also get iced tea, coffee, milk,

00:11:09.633 --> 00:11:11.666
and hot chocolate.

00:11:11.666 --> 00:11:12.933
I think Shake Shack has one more point

00:11:12.933 --> 00:11:13.766
for the soft drinks.

00:11:13.766 --> 00:11:14.600
They look pretty good,

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:16.433
and if you describe
something as "like tea,"

00:11:16.433 --> 00:11:17.400
I'm going to vote for it.

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.166
We cannot forget about the milkshakes.

00:11:19.166 --> 00:11:21.333
I love Shake Shack milkshakes.

00:11:21.333 --> 00:11:22.833
They have their core flavors

00:11:22.833 --> 00:11:24.500
that are always on the menu.

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:25.900
Vanilla, chocolate,

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:28.000
which also has a non-dairy option,

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.133
vanilla-and-chocolate, strawberry,

00:11:30.133 --> 00:11:31.100
black-and-white,

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:32.400
and cookies and cream.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.500
They do seasonal flavors pretty often.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.866
Right now, they have the
triple chocolate brownie shake

00:11:36.866 --> 00:11:38.800
and the Oreo cookie funnel cake shake.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.133
The black-and-white shake

00:11:40.133 --> 00:11:41.866
and the chocolate-and-vanilla shake

00:11:41.866 --> 00:11:43.533
are actually different things.

00:11:43.533 --> 00:11:45.266
I didn't realize this at first.

00:11:45.266 --> 00:11:47.033
But this is the black-and-white shake.

00:11:47.033 --> 00:11:49.733
This is vanilla custard with fudge syrup

00:11:49.733 --> 00:11:50.833
mixed all up in there,

00:11:50.833 --> 00:11:52.933
which gives it a little chocolatey taste.

00:11:52.933 --> 00:11:54.066
I just feel like it's going to taste

00:11:54.066 --> 00:11:55.433
like a chocolate milkshake.

00:11:55.433 --> 00:11:57.433
I don't really get why
it's its own flavor.

00:11:57.433 --> 00:11:59.466
The vanilla-and-chocolate shake flavor

00:11:59.466 --> 00:12:00.733
is just the vanilla custard

00:12:00.733 --> 00:12:02.633
and the chocolate custard mixed together.

00:12:02.633 --> 00:12:04.300
I'm actually going to take a sip

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.533
of the regular chocolate milkshake, too.

00:12:07.533 --> 00:12:09.100
This one tastes slightly different.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.200
I feel like the black-and-white

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:14.500
and possibly the vanilla-and-chocolate

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.333
just taste very, very similar.

00:12:16.333 --> 00:12:18.000
They shouldn't be two separate flavors.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.166
But the chocolate milkshake

00:12:19.166 --> 00:12:20.733
tastes like I'm drinking
chocolate ice cream.

00:12:20.733 --> 00:12:21.866
It's really, really good.

00:12:21.866 --> 00:12:23.733
I do want to taste the non-dairy.

00:12:23.733 --> 00:12:25.900
I've never had a non-dairy
milkshake before.

00:12:27.066 --> 00:12:27.900
No.

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:30.500
It kind of just tastes
like chocolate almond milk.

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:31.733
Not for me.

00:12:31.733 --> 00:12:35.800
I believe this one is the
Oreo cookie funnel cake shake.

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:37.166
It sounds like a lot.

00:12:37.166 --> 00:12:38.833
I just feel like I have so many

00:12:38.833 --> 00:12:40.800
chocolate shakes sitting
in front of me right now,

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:43.133
and they're all starting to
blend together in my mouth.

00:12:43.133 --> 00:12:44.900
I don't know what this tastes like,

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:46.200
but it's not very good.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.366
They do make floats, too.

00:12:47.366 --> 00:12:48.600
I love a good float.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:50.333
This is the Creamsicle flavor.

00:12:50.333 --> 00:12:54.100
I believe it's radioactive orange.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:56.466
I don't know why it's so orange.

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:58.566
Yeah, that's really good.

00:12:58.566 --> 00:13:02.466
And this one is the
classic root beer float.

00:13:02.466 --> 00:13:03.533
Delicious.

00:13:03.533 --> 00:13:07.166
It tastes so good with the
vanilla custard specifically.

00:13:07.166 --> 00:13:09.733
If you want something more
classically dessert-y,

00:13:09.733 --> 00:13:11.200
you can get their frozen custard,

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:12.766
which comes in vanailla, chocolate,

00:13:12.766 --> 00:13:14.066
or dairy-free chocolate.

00:13:14.066 --> 00:13:17.266
They really love the dairy-free
chocolate at Shake Shack.

00:13:18.433 --> 00:13:19.300
It's a choice.

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:21.900
Let's see how the custard
tastes on its own.

00:13:23.366 --> 00:13:24.200
It's delicious.

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:25.900
The vanilla's really, really good.

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:28.466
This is the dairy-free chocolate custard.

00:13:30.666 --> 00:13:32.100
No.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.366
In-N-Out has three flavors of milkshake:

00:13:34.366 --> 00:13:36.466
vanilla, chocolate, and strawberry.

00:13:36.466 --> 00:13:37.600
But you can mix them together

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:39.866
to create whatever flavor
combination you want.

00:13:39.866 --> 00:13:42.333
I did not do that. I'm a shake purist.

00:13:42.333 --> 00:13:43.166
So I wanted to make sure

00:13:43.166 --> 00:13:45.933
that I got the actual
flavors that they offer.

00:13:47.366 --> 00:13:48.933
This strawberry shake is so good.

00:13:48.933 --> 00:13:50.400
It's so good.

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:51.233
Chocolate.

00:13:52.533 --> 00:13:54.000
That's really good, too.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:54.833
And vanilla.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:57.933
Don't sleep on vanilla.

00:13:57.933 --> 00:13:59.100
People think "Eh, vanilla's basic,"

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.866
but this is a good vanilla shake.

00:14:00.866 --> 00:14:02.800
You can also get a root beer float,

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:04.433
which is root beer,

00:14:04.433 --> 00:14:06.866
and they don't have ice cream on the menu,

00:14:06.866 --> 00:14:09.300
so I'm assuming it's vanilla shake.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:10.900
Whatever it is, it's really good.

00:14:11.966 --> 00:14:13.266
Going after A&amp;W.

00:14:14.566 --> 00:14:15.733
I think it looks like Shake Shack

00:14:15.733 --> 00:14:17.166
has way more milkshake options,

00:14:17.166 --> 00:14:18.766
but I think it's just a
lot of the same flavors

00:14:18.766 --> 00:14:20.200
reused in different ways.

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:21.666
Joe seemed to really enjoy

00:14:21.666 --> 00:14:23.166
the limited options that he had,

00:14:23.166 --> 00:14:26.100
so I think maybe quality over quantity.

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:27.266
But we'll say that you
can both have a point.

00:14:29.266 --> 00:14:30.766
Starting off by comparing the burgers.

00:14:30.766 --> 00:14:33.700
This is an In-N-Out cheeseburger.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:34.900
Iconic.

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:35.800
Look at that.

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:38.533
So we have one patty
with a slice of cheese,

00:14:38.533 --> 00:14:40.700
lot of onion, some lettuce, bun,

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:43.666
and a slice of tomato.

00:14:43.666 --> 00:14:45.966
And we're going to do the
same with the ShackBurger.

00:14:45.966 --> 00:14:46.833
Top bun.

00:14:46.833 --> 00:14:49.033
Our wilted lettuce.

00:14:49.033 --> 00:14:51.066
Two teeny tiny tomatoes.

00:14:51.066 --> 00:14:52.300
And then we have our patty.

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:54.966
Obviously, I cannot separate
the cheese from the patty.

00:14:54.966 --> 00:14:56.700
It's all kind of melted in there.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:58.566
And then we have our bottom bun.

00:14:58.566 --> 00:15:02.333
So a Shack burger is 162 grams.

00:15:02.333 --> 00:15:03.533
Point goes to In-N-Out.

00:15:03.533 --> 00:15:04.533
If that wasn't enough,

00:15:04.533 --> 00:15:06.300
at In-N-Out you can also
get a Double-Double,

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:07.366
which is two patties

00:15:07.366 --> 00:15:08.566
and two slices of cheese,

00:15:08.566 --> 00:15:09.400
a 3x3,

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:10.233
which is three patties

00:15:10.233 --> 00:15:11.300
and three slices of cheese,

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:12.333
and a 4x4, which is,

00:15:12.333 --> 00:15:14.066
you guessed it, four patties

00:15:14.066 --> 00:15:15.833
and four slices of cheese.

00:15:15.833 --> 00:15:18.066
The Shack Burger is also
offered as a double,

00:15:18.066 --> 00:15:20.233
so you get two patties instead of one.

00:15:20.233 --> 00:15:22.100
Which chain gives you the
biggest amount of fries?

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.733
Here is an order of In-N-Out fries,

00:15:23.733 --> 00:15:25.200
and we want to weigh them right now.

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:26.666
99 grams.

00:15:26.666 --> 00:15:29.033
Shake Shack only offers one size of fries.

00:15:29.033 --> 00:15:30.666
Let's see how much they weigh.

00:15:30.666 --> 00:15:34.133
An order of fries at
Shake Shack is 190 grams.

00:15:34.133 --> 00:15:35.533
Shake Shack bringing
it back with the fries.

00:15:35.533 --> 00:15:36.366
That's a point.

00:15:36.366 --> 00:15:39.666
In-N-Out gives you four
fountain-drink sizes,

00:15:39.666 --> 00:15:42.433
the small, the medium, the large,

00:15:42.433 --> 00:15:43.566
and the extra large.

00:15:43.566 --> 00:15:45.066
The small at In-N-Out.

00:15:45.066 --> 00:15:46.433
Let's do 12.

00:15:46.433 --> 00:15:47.266
And the medium,

00:15:47.266 --> 00:15:48.800
18 to 19.

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:50.600
We'll be generous and do 19.

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:52.500
Eh, let's do 18. Because
it wouldn't be 19, right?

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:53.333
18.

00:15:53.333 --> 00:15:54.366
I mean, this looks like it would be

00:15:54.366 --> 00:15:55.900
an extra large in most places.

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:57.066
A lot.

00:15:57.066 --> 00:15:59.200
Between 28 and 30.

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:01.633
If only there was a
number between 28 and 30.

00:16:01.633 --> 00:16:03.566
The extra large at In-N-Out.

00:16:03.566 --> 00:16:05.600
Oh, it's exactly 40 ounces.

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:07.900
Yo!

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:09.900
Drinks at Shake Shack come in two sizes,

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:11.466
small and large.

00:16:11.466 --> 00:16:13.333
Let's see how much we
get in the large size.

00:16:13.333 --> 00:16:16.466
This is one of the smaller large drinks

00:16:16.466 --> 00:16:20.033
I've ever seen from a
fast food casual chain.

00:16:20.033 --> 00:16:22.233
So this is 24 ounces of soda.

00:16:22.233 --> 00:16:24.533
The large drink comes out to about

00:16:24.533 --> 00:16:27.233
a little under 700 milliliters,

00:16:27.233 --> 00:16:28.566
or 24 ounces.

00:16:28.566 --> 00:16:30.800
I'm reluctantly giving the
point to In-N-Out there,

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.900
because I think 40
ounces, too much liquid.

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:33.933
24 is more normal,

00:16:33.933 --> 00:16:35.700
but, hey, rules are rules.

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:38.166
Both chains offer milkshakes in one size.

00:16:38.166 --> 00:16:40.033
Let's see how much milkshake
you get at In-N-Out.

00:16:40.033 --> 00:16:42.200
From here, it looks like
it's exactly 16 ounces.

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:44.100
Good for you, In-N-Out.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:47.000
Let's see how much milkshake
you get at Shake Shack.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:51.033
I think that this is 450
milliliters of milkshake,

00:16:51.033 --> 00:16:52.600
almost exactly.

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:55.133
Shake Shack milkshake
slightly bigger. One point.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:00.366
I think it's fair to
say that with fast food,

00:17:00.366 --> 00:17:02.233
people want value for their money.

00:17:02.233 --> 00:17:03.800
We're going to compare some prices

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:06.100
and assign points based on
how much food you're getting

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:07.133
for what you pay.

00:17:07.133 --> 00:17:10.533
An In-N-Out cheeseburger
will cost you $3.75.

00:17:10.533 --> 00:17:11.966
That is shockingly cheap.

00:17:11.966 --> 00:17:15.233
A cheeseburger at Shake
Shack will cost you $7.49.

00:17:15.233 --> 00:17:19.100
OK, so the whole cheeseburger
was 194 grams from earlier,

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:20.533
remember that?

00:17:20.533 --> 00:17:22.133
So per 100, that's,

00:17:22.133 --> 00:17:24.433
OK, divide the price by
the total gram weight,

00:17:24.433 --> 00:17:26.000
which is 194,

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:28.400
but then I multiply that by 100.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.800
So that means it's $1.93 per 100 grams.

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:33.966
A regular cheeseburger at
Shake Shack comes out to

00:17:33.966 --> 00:17:35.733
around 138 grams,

00:17:35.733 --> 00:17:38.000
meaning that it's about $0.05 per gram,

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:41.566
or $5.42 per 100 grams.

00:17:41.566 --> 00:17:43.366
The order of fries that we got at In-N-Out

00:17:43.366 --> 00:17:45.133
was $2.30.

00:17:45.133 --> 00:17:47.533
Honestly, they should be
paying me to eat these fries.

00:17:47.533 --> 00:17:49.900
Anyway, let's also find
out how much it costs

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:51.000
per 100 grams.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.333
It was 99 grams, which was $2.30.

00:17:54.333 --> 00:17:57.166
A fry is not even a gram.

00:17:57.166 --> 00:18:01.966
Can we just say it's $2.30 for 100 grams?

00:18:01.966 --> 00:18:03.500
We've all collectively
agreed that we're fine,

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:07.133
so it's $2.30 for 100 grams.

00:18:07.133 --> 00:18:11.000
At Shake Shack, an order
of fries costs $4.09.

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.866
An order of fries comes
out to about 190 grams,

00:18:13.866 --> 00:18:15.733
making it $0.02 per gram,

00:18:15.733 --> 00:18:18.766
or $2.15 per 100 grams.

00:18:18.766 --> 00:18:20.866
In-N-Out does seem ridiculously cheap.

00:18:20.866 --> 00:18:22.300
I think that's worth a point.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.733
Let's compare nutritional value of items

00:18:26.733 --> 00:18:28.400
that are most similar.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:30.500
A ShackBurger is 500 calories

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:32.566
and contains 30 grams total fat,

00:18:32.566 --> 00:18:34.033
12 grams saturated fat,

00:18:34.033 --> 00:18:36.133
105 milligrams of cholesterol,

00:18:36.133 --> 00:18:39.833
and 1,250 milligrams of sodium.

00:18:39.833 --> 00:18:42.733
An In-N-Out cheeseburger is 480 calories

00:18:42.733 --> 00:18:45.733
and contains 27 grams of total fat,

00:18:45.733 --> 00:18:47.400
10 grams of saturated fat,

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:49.100
60 milligrams of cholesterol,

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:52.066
and 1,000 milligrams of sodium.

00:18:52.066 --> 00:18:53.333
The most calorific items

00:18:53.333 --> 00:18:54.866
on the Shake Shack menu right now

00:18:54.866 --> 00:18:57.833
are the Shake Stack at 770 calories,

00:18:57.833 --> 00:19:01.266
the spicy cheese fries
with ranch at 870 calories,

00:19:01.266 --> 00:19:05.600
and the Oreo cookie funnel
cake shake at 1,080 calories.

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:10.533
For most calorific items on
the official In-N-Out menu,

00:19:10.533 --> 00:19:13.066
we saw online that the
Double-Double with onions

00:19:13.066 --> 00:19:14.700
is 670 calories,

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:18.066
and the strawberry shake,
the regular 15- or 16-ounce,

00:19:18.066 --> 00:19:20.200
is 590 calories.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:24.066
Now, as you are aware,
In-N-Out has a secret menu,

00:19:24.066 --> 00:19:25.300
not-so-secret menu,

00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:28.700
so these calories we found
on third-party sites,

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:31.100
so can't confirm that this is 100% true.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:33.500
But according to smart
people on the internet,

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:37.866
the 4x4 burger is 1,470 calories,

00:19:37.866 --> 00:19:41.000
the animal-style fries is 750 calories,

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:42.833
and

00:19:42.833 --> 00:19:45.766
if you get an extra-large
strawberry shake,

00:19:45.766 --> 00:19:48.200
it's 1,180 calories.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.866
I'm not giving any points
out for the nutrition.

00:19:49.866 --> 00:19:51.300
Live your life. I don't care.

00:19:55.266 --> 00:19:56.166
When it comes to ingredients,

00:19:56.166 --> 00:19:58.366
In-N-Out prides itself on not freezing,

00:19:58.366 --> 00:20:00.966
prepackaging, or
microwaving any of its food.

00:20:00.966 --> 00:20:02.766
This actually might be the exact reason

00:20:02.766 --> 00:20:04.500
why the fries have such a bad rap.

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:06.333
People really hate the
In-N-Out fries, yes,

00:20:06.333 --> 00:20:07.933
including chef David Chang,

00:20:07.933 --> 00:20:10.100
who speculates it's because
they don't freeze their fries

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.766
when the potatoes are in peak season.

00:20:11.766 --> 00:20:14.300
They eventually have to use
potatoes that are out of season,

00:20:14.300 --> 00:20:15.500
and therefore not as good.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:17.233
But then again, they're always bad,

00:20:17.233 --> 00:20:18.100
so I don't know about that theory.

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:20.466
Other theories on why In-N-Out
fries aren't very good

00:20:20.466 --> 00:20:22.000
include the type of potato that are used

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:24.366
and the way the fries are fried.

00:20:24.366 --> 00:20:26.866
They supposedly use Kennebec potatoes,

00:20:26.866 --> 00:20:28.100
which is definitely a unique choice

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:29.200
for fast food restaurants.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:31.266
The go-to is russet potatoes.

00:20:31.266 --> 00:20:33.633
While Shake Shack burgers are made fresh,

00:20:33.633 --> 00:20:36.600
their infamous crinkle-cut
fries are frozen.

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:39.300
In 2013, they actually
switched from the frozen

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:41.133
Yukon Gold crinkle-cut fries

00:20:41.133 --> 00:20:43.600
to hand-cut fries made
from russet potatoes.

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:46.200
Not only were these
fries way harder to make,

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:48.566
but people also just didn't like them.

00:20:48.566 --> 00:20:51.566
I'm not kidding, there was
even a change.org petition.

00:20:51.566 --> 00:20:54.200
They ended up switching back
to the frozen crinkle-cut fries

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:55.633
in the fall of 2014.

00:20:55.633 --> 00:20:57.866
But this time, they worked
with their manufacturer

00:20:57.866 --> 00:21:00.700
to remove the artificial
ingredients and preservatives.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:03.600
I'll admit I don't love Shake Shack fries.

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:06.100
I'm not a crinkle-cut kind of girl.

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:08.800
I'm mainly there for
the burgers and shakes.

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:11.333
But good on them for giving
the people what they wanted.

00:21:11.333 --> 00:21:13.166
As for the meat used for in the burgers,

00:21:13.166 --> 00:21:14.733
Shake Shack uses a custom blend

00:21:14.733 --> 00:21:16.633
of 100% Angus beef.

00:21:16.633 --> 00:21:20.133
And In-N-Out uses 100% USDA ground chuck.

00:21:20.133 --> 00:21:22.666
Shake Shack burgers are famously served

00:21:22.666 --> 00:21:24.266
on Martin's potato rolls.

00:21:24.266 --> 00:21:26.866
If you've ever been to
a Shake Shack in person,

00:21:26.866 --> 00:21:29.233
you can see rows and rows

00:21:29.233 --> 00:21:30.900
of Martin's potato rolls in the back.

00:21:30.900 --> 00:21:32.600
The owners, the Martin family,

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:35.300
were exposed in 2020 for backing far-right

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:37.866
Pennsylvania state Sen. Doug Mastriano,

00:21:37.866 --> 00:21:39.800
who was seen crossing police lines

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:42.533
during the January 6th
attack on the Capitol.

00:21:42.533 --> 00:21:45.566
In 2022, a representative
for Shake Shack told Insider,

00:21:45.566 --> 00:21:47.700
"In regards to the actions of individuals

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:49.700
associated with the Martin's company

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:51.900
and their personal political donations,

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:53.833
those are the choices of those individuals

00:21:53.833 --> 00:21:56.100
and do not express the
values of Shake Shack.

00:21:56.100 --> 00:21:58.700
We continue to be in active
conversations with Martin's

00:21:58.700 --> 00:22:00.433
to expression our concern."

00:22:00.433 --> 00:22:02.333
Switching to another potato roll

00:22:02.333 --> 00:22:04.333
seems to like a very easy thing to do

00:22:04.333 --> 00:22:07.266
for a multibillion-dollar
company like Shake Shack,

00:22:07.266 --> 00:22:08.366
but what do I know?

00:22:08.366 --> 00:22:10.133
In-N-Out gets their
buns from Puritan Bakery

00:22:10.133 --> 00:22:12.100
in Carson, California.

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:13.800
The buns are made by using the sponge

00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:14.633
and dough process,

00:22:14.633 --> 00:22:16.933
which produces buns that
can withstand condiments

00:22:16.933 --> 00:22:18.766
and meat juice without falling apart.

00:22:18.766 --> 00:22:21.100
Another Shake Shack
ingredient I have to mention

00:22:21.100 --> 00:22:23.900
is the frozen custard
that they make in-house.

00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:25.866
I'm calling it an ingredient right now

00:22:25.866 --> 00:22:28.366
because it serves as a base
for all of their milkshakes,

00:22:28.366 --> 00:22:31.233
and I swear, this is
why they taste so good.

00:22:31.233 --> 00:22:33.466
Milkshakes are typically
made with ice cream.

00:22:33.466 --> 00:22:36.233
Frozen custard has all the
same ingredients as ice cream,

00:22:36.233 --> 00:22:38.500
except it also includes egg yolks.

00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:41.766
So using frozen custard gives
you an even richer milkshake.

00:22:41.766 --> 00:22:43.766
The milkshakes at Shake Shack are dense

00:22:43.766 --> 00:22:45.666
and sometimes hard to drink with a straw,

00:22:45.666 --> 00:22:47.266
but they taste so good.

00:22:51.066 --> 00:22:53.266
In-N-Out was founded in 1948

00:22:53.266 --> 00:22:55.133
in Baldwin Park, California.

00:22:55.133 --> 00:22:57.233
And Shake Shack started
out as a hot dog stand

00:22:57.233 --> 00:22:59.433
in Madison Square Park in 2001.

00:22:59.433 --> 00:23:02.800
It officially became the Shake
Shack we know today in 2004.

00:23:02.800 --> 00:23:04.166
Wow, In-N-Out's got
some history behind it.

00:23:04.166 --> 00:23:05.133
That's got to be worth a point.

00:23:05.133 --> 00:23:07.566
In-N-Out has 392 locations in the US,

00:23:07.566 --> 00:23:09.966
but all those locations
are only in seven states:

00:23:09.966 --> 00:23:13.866
California, Texas, Arizona, Nevada, Utah,

00:23:13.866 --> 00:23:15.500
Colorado, and Oregon.

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:19.966
California has the most
locations by far, with 271.

00:23:19.966 --> 00:23:22.500
That means 69% of all In-N-Outs in the US

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:23.766
are in California.

00:23:23.766 --> 00:23:25.366
Nice.

00:23:25.366 --> 00:23:26.800
From the time of filming this,

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:29.966
Shake Shack has 299 locations in the US.

00:23:29.966 --> 00:23:31.733
They're not region-specific

00:23:31.733 --> 00:23:33.800
the way that In-N-Out
is on the West Coast,

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:36.366
but most Shake Shacks
are on the East Coast.

00:23:36.366 --> 00:23:38.533
New York has the most locations, with 49,

00:23:38.533 --> 00:23:40.933
but California is catching
up really quickly.

00:23:40.933 --> 00:23:43.033
They currently have 40 locations.

00:23:43.033 --> 00:23:45.700
Shake Shack is also available
in over 80 countries.

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:48.433
There are over 400 locations worldwide.

00:23:48.433 --> 00:23:49.566
I think Shake Shack gets a point there

00:23:49.566 --> 00:23:50.566
for the availability.

00:23:50.566 --> 00:23:51.666
I like the fact that it's available

00:23:51.666 --> 00:23:53.933
not just on the East Coast, but elsewhere,

00:23:53.933 --> 00:23:55.300
and even here in the UK

00:23:55.300 --> 00:23:56.633
and other parts of the world.

00:23:56.633 --> 00:23:58.766
For the most part, I
think these two chains

00:23:58.766 --> 00:24:00.100
do exist peacefully,

00:24:00.100 --> 00:24:02.000
and I think that's
because they're actually

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.566
not very similar.

00:24:03.566 --> 00:24:06.500
In-N-Out feels like
this constant, reliable

00:24:06.500 --> 00:24:08.366
fast food chain,

00:24:08.366 --> 00:24:09.933
and Shake Shack is a fine casual chain

00:24:09.933 --> 00:24:11.233
that's constantly adding

00:24:11.233 --> 00:24:13.033
and removing things from its menu.

00:24:13.033 --> 00:24:14.800
They do a lot of seasonal stuff.

00:24:14.800 --> 00:24:18.200
The rivalry is something we
as the customers created.

00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:20.200
Everyone loves to compare these two.

00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:21.333
You know, I didn't really think there was

00:24:21.333 --> 00:24:24.200
much of a beef between
Shake Shack and In-N-Out.

00:24:24.200 --> 00:24:25.500
Me personally, if I want Shake Shack,

00:24:25.500 --> 00:24:26.333
I want In-N-Out,

00:24:26.333 --> 00:24:28.033
I feel like the two don't really overlap

00:24:28.033 --> 00:24:29.633
as far as what I want from either one.

00:24:29.633 --> 00:24:31.533
That's my personal opinion.

00:24:31.533 --> 00:24:32.900
I understand it's two businesses

00:24:32.900 --> 00:24:34.300
that are competing.

00:24:34.300 --> 00:24:37.800
But I think both have coexisted just fine.

00:24:37.800 --> 00:24:39.500
Both chains give off different vibes

00:24:39.500 --> 00:24:42.666
that I do think are
inspired by their regions.

00:24:42.666 --> 00:24:44.900
In-N-Out gives me more laid-back,

00:24:44.900 --> 00:24:46.800
beachy Americana.

00:24:46.800 --> 00:24:48.900
Shake Shack feels more minimalist

00:24:48.900 --> 00:24:50.633
and muted and modern.

00:24:50.633 --> 00:24:53.266
In-N-Out still feels like a traditional

00:24:53.266 --> 00:24:54.833
fast food restaurant.

00:24:54.833 --> 00:24:55.666
Yes you can eat there,

00:24:55.666 --> 00:24:58.366
but the vibe is definitely,
hit the drive-thru and go.

00:24:58.366 --> 00:25:01.166
Shake Shack is for sure
on the pricier side.

00:25:01.166 --> 00:25:04.600
My go-to order usually
comes out to about $17.

00:25:04.600 --> 00:25:09.000
That's $17 for a bacon cheeseburger,
fries, and a milkshake.

00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:11.366
The founder described the
concept for Shake Shack

00:25:11.366 --> 00:25:13.100
as "fine casual,"

00:25:13.100 --> 00:25:15.700
so they're not shying away
from how pricey it is.

00:25:15.700 --> 00:25:18.033
This food was less expensive

00:25:18.033 --> 00:25:20.833
than almost all the fast food
we've covered on Food Wars.

00:25:20.833 --> 00:25:25.866
Also, we got a little over $100
worth of food for this shoot.

00:25:26.300 --> 00:25:28.333
It took them maybe seven
minutes to fill that order.

00:25:28.333 --> 00:25:29.300
I didn't call ahead.

00:25:29.300 --> 00:25:30.866
Went in there, got everything.

00:25:30.866 --> 00:25:32.733
Listen, I've had both,

00:25:32.733 --> 00:25:35.200
and even though taste
is obviously subjective,

00:25:35.200 --> 00:25:38.333
I just think Shake Shack's
burger tastes better.

00:25:38.333 --> 00:25:40.233
If you put both burgers in front of me

00:25:40.233 --> 00:25:42.200
without me knowing anything about them,

00:25:42.200 --> 00:25:43.800
I would always pick the Shake Shack burger

00:25:43.800 --> 00:25:45.200
as the better of the two.

00:25:45.200 --> 00:25:47.900
Aside from the delicious crispy burgers,

00:25:47.900 --> 00:25:50.333
I just like how many options
I have at Shake Shack.

00:25:50.333 --> 00:25:52.633
And it's not like they do any one food

00:25:52.633 --> 00:25:53.766
better than the other.

00:25:53.766 --> 00:25:54.600
I think the chicken

00:25:54.600 --> 00:25:56.866
and the vegetarian options are also great.

00:25:56.866 --> 00:25:58.600
The only thing I'm not a huge fan of

00:25:58.600 --> 00:25:59.600
is the plain fries.

00:25:59.600 --> 00:26:00.900
And I still think that they're better

00:26:00.900 --> 00:26:04.133
than the plain fries at In-N-Out, so.

00:26:04.133 --> 00:26:05.500
When people come and
visit me in Los Angeles,

00:26:05.500 --> 00:26:08.433
which is rare, because of my personality,

00:26:08.433 --> 00:26:11.100
they are like, "I want to go to In-N-Out.

00:26:11.100 --> 00:26:12.366
Not with you, Joe,

00:26:12.366 --> 00:26:13.400
but I'm going to go to In-N-Out."

00:26:13.400 --> 00:26:16.266
And then later, I find
out that they enjoyed it,

00:26:16.266 --> 00:26:17.533
thought it was incredible.

